@startuml
title Layer gizmos: pick a layer on the preview and drag it

actor User
participant LayerGizmo
participant LayerGizmoViewModel as Gizmo
participant TimelineEditor
participant CommandHistory
participant PreviewViewModel as Preview

== pick ==
User -> LayerGizmo : press on the picture
LayerGizmo -> Gizmo : handle under the pointer?
alt on a handle or a selected layer
  Gizmo --> LayerGizmo : grab (move / scale / rotate)
else on another layer
  Gizmo -> TimelineEditor : LayerAt(playhead, x, y)  (topmost track first)
  TimelineEditor --> Gizmo : clip
  Gizmo -> TimelineEditor : Selection.Replace(key)  (Ctrl/Shift: Toggle)
  note right: the same selection as a click on the\ntimeline: inspector tabs follow
  Gizmo --> LayerGizmo : grab = move
end
LayerGizmo -> Gizmo : Begin()
Gizmo -> CommandHistory : BreakCoalescing()

== drag ==
loop pointer moves
  LayerGizmo -> Gizmo : Move | Scale | Rotate  (Shift: 15° steps, Ctrl: no snap)
  Gizmo -> Gizmo : each selected layer: its layout at Begin + delta\n(centre snaps to the frame's middle lines)
  Gizmo -> TimelineEditor : SetLayouts(layout per clip)
  TimelineEditor -> CommandHistory : ExecuteCoalescing (one step per drag)
  TimelineEditor --> Preview : TimelineChanged -> frame redrawn
  Gizmo --> LayerGizmo : Items changed -> boxes redrawn
end
User -> LayerGizmo : release
@enduml
